From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:23:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-cheetah: supply the
 fingerprint sensor

The fingerprint sensor's analog supply is S2MPG13 LDO15S
(L15S_UDFPS_AVDD in Google's cheetah device tree). The bootloader hands
over with it off, and stock Android keeps it on only because its device
tree marks it regulator-always-on.

Describe LDO15S under the sub-PMIC with stock's 2.5-3.3 V range, so that
registering it sets nothing unless the rail is outside that range, and
give the sensor node its vdd-supply. The goodix-fp driver then switches
the rail on first open and off on last close, with the sensor held in
reset while unpowered. Both the sub-PMIC and the sensor node stay
disabled by default.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
index a40b5f071..7869064b0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@ fingerprint {
 		interrupt-parent = <&gpa9>;
 		interrupts = <2 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		reset-gpios = <&gpp1 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		vdd-supply = <&ldo15s>;
 		pinctrl-0 = <&fp_irq &fp_reset>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		status = "disabled";
